#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""POSSESSION V3.1 KIT: possession v3.1's file, in ONE self-contained file (ATLAS_QUEUE PART D; a PROVISIONAL CANDIDATE).
GENERATED by build_possession_v3_1_standalone.py from the frozen sources of the team's code folder. Do not edit by
hand; rebuild.

    python possession_v3_1_standalone.py --data "/path/to/data" --out "/path/to/output/folder"

--data is the folder ABOVE "tactical": its tactical/ folder must hold the two tracking files BAR-ATH_tactical_atd.xml
and BAR-ATH_tactical_atd.txt, which is all the run reads. You also need Python with the exact versions pinned below.
The file sets the numerical libraries to one thread, checks those versions, the SHA-256 of every embedded source and
of the embedded models (all trained on public DFL matches only; v2.1's and v2.2's edge models and v2.3's
missed-stoppage detector on RLH's simulated dead ball of those matches, reports 0230, 0247 and 0265; v2.4's evidence
model and reader on the organisers' written possession convention of those matches, report 0273; v2.5 adds a rule,
no model: the merged-stoppage splitter, report 0326; v2.6 adds a rule, no model: the false-stoppage
re-opening, report 0343; v2.7 changes one constant, no model: the contest push at B 1.5, report 0365; v2.8 adds a WM-trained evidence
model blended at 0.4, the decoder price x1.41, the contest push OFF and an RLH-trained set-up classifier that keeps
restarts dead while the players set up, report 0392; v2.8-NS is v2.8 with set-up mode OFF: the set-up
classifier stays embedded and checked but is never loaded, report 0394; v2.9 loads it again, with the hold stopped at
the first shown kick, report 0395), the input files and the tracking's 199,319 records. Then it runs the real functions in
their real order: dead ball v1.1 as core_real_run.py and dead_ball_v1_1.py compute it (no labels of any kind are
read), then possession v3.1 as possession_v3_1.py does. It writes OUT/possession_v3_1.csv, byte for byte what
possession_v3_1.py writes, and validates it with the organisers' validation. It prints counts, PASS/FAIL words and a
fingerprint of the file only. Read README_POSSESSION_V3_1_CANDIDATE.txt; the FINGERPRINT must equal the team's
reference (none yet: v3.1 is a candidate).
"""

